--- MODEL OUTPUT ---
The void thins to a silver haze.  
Three cards drift forward and hover chest-high, edges glowing like moonlit glass.

First turns: The High Priestess.  
Her pillared throne faces you, scroll half-open, eyes calm.  
A cool tide rises behind your ribs—quiet, balanced, listening.

Second: Six of Cups.  
Two children on the card offer a flowering cup; pastel chalk still clings to their smudged knees.  
Your own palms tingle with remembered sun-warmth and the scent of crushed grass.

Third: Knight of Pentacles.  
A armored rider holds a single gold coin against brown fields.  
Your heartbeat steadies, hooves drumming slow patience through the soles of your feet.

These cards are now yours. They hum in your memory.

The haze peels away like wet silk.  
Stone replaces void—rough granite under your back, dawn air brushing your face.  
The Awakening begins.

